WEBVTT

00:01.653 --> 00:02.955
<i>PETER:
Valentine's Day:</i>

00:03.055 --> 00:04.305
<i>a day of love,</i>

00:04.340 --> 00:06.457
<i>right in the middle
of Black History Month.</i>

00:06.475 --> 00:08.559
<i>There are a thousand hearts
in Quahog,</i>

00:08.594 --> 00:10.278
<i>a thousand stories.</i>

00:10.312 --> 00:12.397
<i>Some people don't have
any stories.</i>

00:12.431 --> 00:13.965
<i>Others got two.</i>

00:13.983 --> 00:15.416
<i>Anyway, here's a song your
girlfriend probably likes.</i>

00:15.451 --> 00:19.687
♪ I got a feeling

00:19.722 --> 00:22.807
♪ That tonight's gonna be
a good night ♪

00:22.841 --> 00:27.161
♪ That tonight's
gonna be a good night ♪

00:27.196 --> 00:28.813
I'm afraid I have
some terrible news:

00:28.847 --> 00:30.114
(gasps)

00:30.149 --> 00:32.834
I have dinner reservations
and no one to go with.

00:32.868 --> 00:34.786
♪ Tonight's the night

00:34.820 --> 00:36.688
♪ Let's live it up

00:36.722 --> 00:38.656
♪ I got my money

00:38.674 --> 00:41.793
Hi, I'll be
your wife's nurse.

00:41.827 --> 00:42.948
Would you excuse me
a second?

00:45.381 --> 00:46.381
Okay, I'm back.

00:46.415 --> 00:48.316
♪ Here we come,
here we go ♪

00:48.350 --> 00:50.168
♪ We gotta rock

00:50.202 --> 00:52.754
♪ I know that
we'll have a ball ♪

00:52.788 --> 00:54.656
♪ If we get down and go out

00:54.690 --> 00:57.025
♪ And just lose it all

00:57.059 --> 01:00.194
♪ I feel stressed out,
I wanna let it go ♪

01:00.229 --> 01:02.363
♪ Let's go way out, spaced out

01:02.398 --> 01:04.565
♪ Losing all control

01:04.600 --> 01:06.167
♪ Fill up my cup

01:06.201 --> 01:08.519
♪ Mazel tov

01:08.554 --> 01:09.971
♪ Look at her dancing

01:10.005 --> 01:11.539
♪ Just take it

01:11.573 --> 01:12.874
♪ Off.

01:15.577 --> 01:19.664
Peter, are you ready
for your Valentine's gift?

01:20.933 --> 01:23.835
No, but I'm ready for therapy.

01:39.335 --> 01:41.269
Peter, you awake?

01:41.320 --> 01:43.438
It's a beautiful day.

01:43.472 --> 01:45.273
Um, yeah, I'm just glad
I didn't die

01:45.307 --> 01:47.091
from the weird
sleep-breathing thing I have.

01:48.727 --> 01:50.928
(screaming)

01:55.551 --> 01:57.902
You know, Peter, since
it's Valentine's Day

01:57.920 --> 01:59.737
I was thinking
let's do something

01:59.772 --> 02:01.272
we've never
done before.

02:01.306 --> 02:02.990
Release the virus?

02:03.025 --> 02:05.827
No, I was thinking we could
spend the whole day in bed.

02:05.861 --> 02:07.528
Oh, that's a great idea.

02:07.563 --> 02:11.432
Permission to begin a day of
epic lovemaking, sexy lady.

02:11.467 --> 02:13.634
Permission
granted, sir.

02:13.669 --> 02:15.837
<i>PETER: And if I need help,
I'll just fantasize</i>

02:15.871 --> 02:17.939
<i>about that Victorian stripper.</i>

02:17.973 --> 02:19.674
Yeah, you slut.

02:19.708 --> 02:22.593
Doth the magistrate know
what you're doing tonight?

02:22.628 --> 02:23.861
Good.

02:23.896 --> 02:27.415
Now, undo the top six buttons
of your 100-button shoes.

02:33.238 --> 02:34.372
Wow, Meg,
you look nice.

02:34.406 --> 02:35.606
You got a date?

02:35.641 --> 02:38.009
Yeah, I totally hit it
off with this great guy

02:38.043 --> 02:39.963
in the Internet, and we're
finally going to meet.

02:39.978 --> 02:42.080
Okay, remember to ask
questions about him.

02:42.114 --> 02:45.183
Seem interested.
Listen. Giggle.

02:45.217 --> 02:46.467
Swallow.

02:46.502 --> 02:47.485
(doorbell rings)

02:47.519 --> 02:48.619
Oh, my God,
that's him.

02:50.506 --> 02:51.472
Toby?

02:51.507 --> 02:52.623
Meg?

02:52.658 --> 02:55.026
Hi. Wow, you look just
like your picture.

02:55.060 --> 02:57.528
You don't look
anything like yours.

02:59.998 --> 03:02.834
Yeah, that's a candid
from a summer job I had.

03:02.868 --> 03:04.635
Well, you're much
prettier in person.

03:04.670 --> 03:05.636
Shall we go?

03:05.671 --> 03:06.671
Yeah, sure.

03:06.705 --> 03:08.106
Don't wait up, boys.

03:09.725 --> 03:10.758
I like him.

03:10.793 --> 03:12.176
Really? He seems
kind of lame.

03:12.211 --> 03:13.728
But, I guess
every girl

03:13.762 --> 03:15.496
has her own version
of Prince Charming.

03:15.531 --> 03:17.098
I'm in love with Paul.

03:17.132 --> 03:18.566
I'm in love
with John.

03:18.600 --> 03:19.634
You know what?

03:19.668 --> 03:21.369
I'm in love
with Ringo.

03:21.420 --> 03:22.420
What?

03:22.454 --> 03:23.521
Um, I said...

03:23.555 --> 03:24.889
I don't-I don't know
what I said.

03:24.923 --> 03:26.891
Sounded like you said you
were in love with Ringo.

03:26.925 --> 03:29.427
Um, I don't...
I don't think so.

03:29.461 --> 03:31.829
Pretty sure you said
"I'm in love with Ringo."

03:31.864 --> 03:32.964
Here I am.

03:32.998 --> 03:34.265
Are Paul and John
out there?

03:34.299 --> 03:36.150
Nope, just Ringo.

03:42.741 --> 03:44.442
Oh, you're still here?

03:44.476 --> 03:46.277
Yeah, after
a wonderful night

03:46.311 --> 03:48.062
I-I thought we could
get some breakfast.

03:48.113 --> 03:50.715
(laughing): Clearly, you're not
familiar with how this works.

03:50.749 --> 03:52.310
See, you're supposed
to be already gone.

03:52.334 --> 03:53.367
There's no breakfast.

03:53.402 --> 03:55.086
Here, let me help you
to the door.

03:58.407 --> 04:00.191
You're a jerk,
Glenn Quagmire.

04:00.209 --> 04:02.410
One of these days, you're
going to get what you deserve.

04:02.427 --> 04:03.878
You better put
something warm on.

04:03.912 --> 04:06.747
You got an icicle
forming down there.

04:07.983 --> 04:10.168
Dumb broad left her
electric tampon warmer.

04:10.202 --> 04:11.669
(screaming)

04:25.133 --> 04:27.118
What the hell?

04:27.152 --> 04:28.619
That's weird.

04:28.654 --> 04:30.555
Why do I look like a chick
in that mirror?

04:35.827 --> 04:37.144
(screaming)

04:37.179 --> 04:39.614
Ah, what's wrong with you,
Holder-Downer 5000?

04:39.665 --> 04:40.798
That's just for women.

04:43.268 --> 04:44.569
Hold it together, Quagmire.

04:44.603 --> 04:46.687
You probably just had
one too many drinks last night.

04:46.722 --> 04:47.738
(siren blaring)

04:47.756 --> 04:48.973
Son of a bitch.

04:55.531 --> 04:56.764
Ah, hey, Joe.

04:56.798 --> 04:58.866
God, I thought
I was in trouble for a minute.

04:58.901 --> 05:00.735
Hey, toots, you know
why I pulled you over?

05:00.769 --> 05:02.603
You were going too
sexy in a 35 zone.

05:02.638 --> 05:03.971
I'll need to see
your driver's license.

05:04.006 --> 05:05.006
What?

05:05.040 --> 05:06.541
Joe, what the hell's
wrong with you?

05:06.575 --> 05:07.558
It's me, Quagmire.

05:07.593 --> 05:09.594
JOE:
Glenda Vajmire.

05:09.628 --> 05:11.662
Well, how would you
like to spend four hours

05:11.697 --> 05:14.532
desperately trying to
give me a muscular soldier?

05:14.566 --> 05:15.750
What the hell,
you weirdo?

05:15.784 --> 05:16.751
(laughing)

05:16.785 --> 05:18.152
I'm just having fun.

05:18.186 --> 05:21.172
In fact, as I say to all
the ladies, giggity-giggity.

05:21.206 --> 05:22.873
You don't say that.
I say that.

05:22.908 --> 05:24.041
You're a bad person.

05:32.768 --> 05:33.935
Hey, Stewie,
what are you doing?

05:33.969 --> 05:35.970
Well, Brian, in honor
of Valentine's Day

05:36.004 --> 05:37.705
I thought why not
go back in time

05:37.739 --> 05:39.607
to that summer of love
in the '60s

05:39.641 --> 05:40.908
that everyone's always
talking about.

05:40.943 --> 05:42.176
Oh, cool.

05:42.210 --> 05:44.528
Hey, you think you might be
able to get me some acid?

05:44.546 --> 05:46.063
I'll get you rolled-up
newspaper on the snout

05:46.098 --> 05:47.214
is what I'll get you.

05:47.249 --> 05:49.083
Very. Bad. Dog.

05:56.592 --> 05:59.927
Well, here we are, Rupert:
Quahog's summer of love.

05:59.962 --> 06:04.131
♪

06:08.070 --> 06:10.705
Ball, please.

06:16.227 --> 06:17.778
Hello.

06:17.813 --> 06:18.980
Oh, this must be yours.

06:19.014 --> 06:20.348
Thanks.

06:20.382 --> 06:22.783
My God, she's incredible.

06:22.818 --> 06:25.519
Rupert, I must bring her
back to the present

06:25.554 --> 06:27.121
and raise her to be my wife.

06:28.073 --> 06:31.208
Oh, God, I bet that diaper
is soaking wet.

06:32.778 --> 06:34.829
I can't let her get away.

06:37.049 --> 06:38.232
Oh, hi.

06:38.266 --> 06:41.535
Oh, hey, um, I just
came to say, um...

06:41.570 --> 06:44.805
you know, in a couple of years
something's going to come along

06:44.840 --> 06:45.840
called Sesame Street.

06:45.874 --> 06:47.775
And I know the name
makes it sounds Asian,

06:47.809 --> 06:50.211
but it's not, and it's
going to blow your mind.

06:50.245 --> 06:51.545
Oh, the hell with it.

06:51.580 --> 06:53.481
The real reason I ran
over here is because

06:53.515 --> 06:56.283
I wanted to do this.

06:56.318 --> 06:59.737
There's my little Lois.

06:59.771 --> 07:00.805
What?

07:00.839 --> 07:01.872
Lois?!

07:01.907 --> 07:03.607
Come on, honey.
Hop in Daddy's car.

07:03.642 --> 07:04.942
You can crawl around
on the floor

07:04.976 --> 07:06.610
while I drink, smoke,
and drive us home.

07:07.295 --> 07:10.748
(hyperventilating)

07:17.339 --> 07:20.041
(gagging)

07:20.075 --> 07:21.342
Oh, my God, Stewie,
what happened?

07:21.376 --> 07:23.044
None of your (bleep)
business what happened.

07:23.078 --> 07:25.112
Geez, you kiss your mother
with that mouth?

07:33.088 --> 07:34.505
Do you like Coldplay?

07:34.539 --> 07:36.173
Uh, am I a dull
white guy?

07:36.208 --> 07:37.541
Yes, I like Coldplay.

07:37.576 --> 07:40.644
God, Toby, I can't believe
how much we have in common.

07:40.679 --> 07:42.947
It's like we were meant
to find each other.

07:42.981 --> 07:44.031
I know.

07:44.066 --> 07:45.149
To us.

07:45.183 --> 07:46.784
Meg, if you were
any more beautiful,

07:46.818 --> 07:48.185
that'd be neat.

07:50.222 --> 07:52.656
So, what should be do next...

07:57.946 --> 07:59.480
(screaming)

07:59.531 --> 08:00.865
Oh, my God!

08:00.899 --> 08:02.867
Toby, what happened?

08:02.901 --> 08:05.436
Oh, I just harvested
your kidney.

08:05.470 --> 08:07.204
(gasps) Look at the
size of this scar.

08:07.239 --> 08:10.074
Sorry. It's my first day
on this job.

08:10.108 --> 08:11.876
Well, where did
you work before?

08:11.910 --> 08:12.977
Circuit City.

08:13.011 --> 08:14.979
So, I haven't worked
in, like, two years.

08:21.729 --> 08:23.663
Toby, I can't believe
you took my kidney.

08:23.697 --> 08:24.964
You bastard!

08:24.999 --> 08:26.032
Sorry, Meg.

08:26.066 --> 08:27.400
Black market organs
are big money

08:27.434 --> 08:29.402
and I promised my bosses
a fresh kidney.

08:29.436 --> 08:30.937
No hard feelings.

08:30.971 --> 08:31.938
Wait!

08:31.972 --> 08:34.240
You also made
a promise to me.

08:34.274 --> 08:36.609
You promised we'd spend
Valentine's Day together.

08:36.643 --> 08:38.344
The whole day.

08:38.395 --> 08:40.730
And I'm not letting you
break that promise.

08:40.764 --> 08:42.899
Well, I guess a deal's a deal.

08:42.933 --> 08:44.133
Okay.

08:45.669 --> 08:48.538
By the way, did you know
you had a tiny conjoined twin

08:48.572 --> 08:49.572
attached to your hip?

08:51.141 --> 08:52.208
Is it worth anything?

08:52.242 --> 08:53.342
It is to me.

08:53.377 --> 08:54.810
I've been using it
as a bookmark.

09:01.919 --> 09:03.453
Peter, what's all this?

09:03.487 --> 09:05.755
<i>Oh, Quagmire loaned me this book
called the Kama Sutra.</i>

09:05.789 --> 09:06.789
It's Indian.

09:06.823 --> 09:08.207
And who has better sex

09:08.258 --> 09:10.476
than people who don't
use toilet paper?

09:10.511 --> 09:13.229
I don't know, Peter.
That doesn't sound very sexy.

09:13.263 --> 09:14.347
What are you
talking about?

09:14.381 --> 09:15.498
Bombay is sperm city.

09:15.516 --> 09:17.316
<i>Slumdog Millionaire?</i>

09:17.351 --> 09:20.019
<i>More like
Scumdog Put-it-there.</i>

09:20.054 --> 09:22.889
Peter, these candles are
getting wax all over the floor.

09:22.940 --> 09:24.507
That's okay. Isn't
Consuela coming today?

09:24.525 --> 09:27.744
No, she spends Valentine's Day
with her husband.

09:38.756 --> 09:40.873
<i>Wait, but she's sneaking
out of the U.S.</i>

09:40.908 --> 09:42.208
This is Arizona.

09:42.242 --> 09:44.460
You can shoot a Mexican
for using a water fountain.

09:48.265 --> 09:49.315
(dress rips)

09:49.349 --> 09:51.117
Oh, I fix later.

09:53.053 --> 09:54.470
(sirens blaring)

09:56.340 --> 09:58.341
Happy Valentine's
Day, Juan.

09:58.375 --> 10:00.243
<i>And to you, mi amor.</i>

10:00.277 --> 10:02.578
One minute, I
freshen up first.

10:05.516 --> 10:07.483
Okay.

10:07.518 --> 10:11.720
<i>CONSUELA:
SГ­, sГ­, sГ­... oh, yeah.</i>

10:20.147 --> 10:21.247
Hi.

10:21.281 --> 10:24.917
Oh, hey, um, I think I might
have the wrong address.

10:24.952 --> 10:26.819
I'm looking for
Mr. Herbert's house.

10:26.854 --> 10:28.287
No, you're at
the right house.

10:28.322 --> 10:30.256
I'm his grandniece,
Sandy.

10:30.290 --> 10:32.525
Wow, my name
is Chris, too.

10:32.559 --> 10:35.928
Oh, hey, there, Chris,
happy Valentine's Day.

10:35.963 --> 10:39.499
Hope cupid brings you
a saggy old bag of treats.

10:39.533 --> 10:42.435
Hey, Mr. Herbert, I'm just here
to collect for the newspaper.

10:42.469 --> 10:44.237
Here you go.

10:44.271 --> 10:48.141
Oh, hang now, Chris.
Your fly's up again.

10:48.175 --> 10:49.742
Thanks, Mr. Herbert.

10:52.129 --> 10:54.430
He's so hot.

10:54.464 --> 10:55.832
(sighing):
I'd love to talk to him,

10:55.866 --> 10:57.733
but I just don't know
what I would say.

10:57.768 --> 10:59.769
Oh, I know all
the things to say.

10:59.803 --> 11:01.304
Maybe I can
help you out.

11:01.338 --> 11:02.505
You'd do that for me?

11:02.539 --> 11:03.606
Sure.

11:03.640 --> 11:05.608
Right after my
favorite show.

11:05.642 --> 11:07.076
<i>Coming up next:</i>

11:07.110 --> 11:10.513
To Catch a Predator
Who's Proud of Being a Predator.

11:10.547 --> 11:11.781
Good evening, sir.

11:11.815 --> 11:13.282
<i>I'm Chris Hansen
with Dateline.</i>

11:13.317 --> 11:15.651
Do you know the boy you were
coming here to meet tonight

11:15.686 --> 11:18.020
is only 13 years old?

11:18.055 --> 11:19.555
No, I drove
900 (bleep) miles

11:19.590 --> 11:21.357
for a 14-year-old.

11:24.428 --> 11:26.329
So what seems
to be the trouble?

11:26.363 --> 11:28.014
Dr. Hartman,
something's wrong with me!

11:28.065 --> 11:29.682
Everyone's treating me
like I'm a broad!

11:29.716 --> 11:31.083
I-I don't know
what's going on!

11:31.118 --> 11:33.319
I recognize that
hysterical tone of voice.

11:33.353 --> 11:34.687
Sounds like someone's
having their monthly.

11:34.721 --> 11:37.256
All right, sweetie,
let me just spit on my hand,

11:37.291 --> 11:38.307
and we'll get started.

11:38.325 --> 11:40.359
Ah! Get away from me,
you creep!

11:42.713 --> 11:44.163
(gasps)
My God!

11:44.198 --> 11:46.065
There was nothing wrong
with my mirror!

11:46.099 --> 11:48.818
Everyone sees me as a woman!
Oh, no!

11:48.852 --> 11:51.487
This is the universe giving me
what I deserve

11:51.521 --> 11:53.656
for being such a pig
all the time!

11:53.674 --> 11:56.642
From now on,
I'm gonna do things differently.

11:56.677 --> 11:58.945
Men are jerks!
Let's swear off of them

11:58.979 --> 12:00.463
and find comfort in each other!

12:00.497 --> 12:02.131
Com here, you guys!

12:02.165 --> 12:04.917
(squeals)

12:08.872 --> 12:09.922
So, what's with you?

12:09.957 --> 12:10.957
No Valentine's Day plans?

12:10.991 --> 12:11.991
(scoffs) No.

12:12.025 --> 12:13.509
I've had it
with Valentine's Day.

12:13.543 --> 12:14.927
I'm sick of all of it.

12:14.962 --> 12:16.562
Okay, I'm putting on
my friend hat.

12:16.597 --> 12:17.964
What's the matter?
Let me in.

12:17.998 --> 12:19.398
I don't know.
It's just...

12:19.433 --> 12:21.500
How come it's so hard
to meet the right woman?

12:21.535 --> 12:23.903
I think maybe it's just time
for me to give up.

12:23.954 --> 12:25.755
Come on, Brian.
You can't give up.

12:25.789 --> 12:27.189
Everything could
change in a moment.

12:27.224 --> 12:29.025
That's what happened with
the Kennedy assassination.

12:29.059 --> 12:31.928
I'm sorry, gentlemen.
Despite our best efforts,

12:31.962 --> 12:34.530
the Texas School Book Depository
Awareness Council has failed

12:34.564 --> 12:36.165
in its mission to generate
public awareness

12:36.199 --> 12:37.700
of the Texas School
Book Depository.

12:37.734 --> 12:39.502
So at the end of the day,

12:39.536 --> 12:40.903
we'll be shutting
down operations

12:40.938 --> 12:42.471
and laying
everyone off.

12:42.506 --> 12:45.374
Sir, I think you're
gonna want to see this!

12:45.409 --> 12:48.494
♪ Let's fall in love

12:48.528 --> 12:51.080
♪ Why shouldn't we fall
in love? ♪

12:51.114 --> 12:53.366
♪ Our hearts are made of it

12:53.417 --> 12:54.500
♪ Let's take a chance

12:54.534 --> 12:58.471
♪ Why be afraid of it?

12:58.505 --> 13:01.524
♪ Let's close our eyes

13:01.558 --> 13:05.144
♪ And make our own paradise

13:05.178 --> 13:07.580
♪ Little we know of it

13:07.614 --> 13:11.550
♪ Still, we can try
to make a go of it ♪

13:11.585 --> 13:14.287
♪ Let's fall in love.

13:25.349 --> 13:26.882
Oh, Brian,
there you are.

13:26.917 --> 13:28.183
Look, I've been
thinking about

13:28.201 --> 13:29.218
your situation
with women,

13:29.252 --> 13:31.253
and I believe
I've come up with a way

13:31.288 --> 13:33.456
to get to the source
of the problem. Follow me.

13:33.490 --> 13:34.824
What's going on?

13:36.026 --> 13:37.426
Oh, my God.

13:39.863 --> 13:40.963
Stewie, what the hell?!

13:40.998 --> 13:42.448
These are all
my ex-girlfriends!

13:42.482 --> 13:44.550
Well, I thought they could
provide some insights

13:44.584 --> 13:46.052
that might improve
your love life.

13:46.086 --> 13:47.453
Ladies, as you may have guessed,

13:47.487 --> 13:49.655
you are here
because you have all dated

13:49.690 --> 13:51.257
this great guy.

13:51.291 --> 13:52.892
Yet, somehow, things
didn't work out.

13:52.926 --> 13:55.027
My objective is
to figure out why.

13:55.062 --> 13:56.262
I don't know.

13:56.296 --> 13:57.730
The word "self-absorbed"
comes to mind.

13:57.764 --> 13:59.131
And pretentious.

13:59.166 --> 14:00.132
Definitely pretentious.

14:00.167 --> 14:02.335
And he's got a big eggo.

14:02.369 --> 14:04.236
Okay, we seem
to have a theme going here.

14:04.271 --> 14:05.738
Oh, come on!
You're all just mad

14:05.772 --> 14:07.039
because I didn't
wanna be with you!

14:07.074 --> 14:08.607
(masculine voice): I think Brian's
a wonderful man.

14:08.642 --> 14:10.343
He's just having
a difficult time

14:10.377 --> 14:12.378
coming to terms
with his own sexuality.

14:12.412 --> 14:14.213
Shut up, Ida.
She's my favorite.

14:14.247 --> 14:15.247
He's insecure.

14:15.282 --> 14:16.415
And a blowhard.

14:16.450 --> 14:18.067
And he's got a tiny penis!

14:18.085 --> 14:19.552
(all laughing)

14:19.586 --> 14:21.604
Yeah, that was pretty clear
by the survey.

14:21.638 --> 14:23.105
Okay, now who wants
more wine?

14:23.140 --> 14:24.090
This is great.

14:24.124 --> 14:25.574
We should do this
every Saturday.

14:25.609 --> 14:27.777
No, no, we're not gonna
do this every Saturday!

14:27.811 --> 14:29.345
What's wrong?
We're just being honest.

14:29.379 --> 14:30.796
Oh, oh, you want honest?!

14:30.831 --> 14:32.465
You're an old bag.
You're blind.

14:32.499 --> 14:33.599
Your vomit tastes weird.

14:33.633 --> 14:34.967
You don't even know
why you're here.

14:35.018 --> 14:36.535
<i>You chose to be
on The Hills.</i>

14:36.570 --> 14:38.204
You still have
bits of penis left,

14:38.238 --> 14:39.438
and you can never get wet.

14:39.473 --> 14:40.806
(whines)

14:40.857 --> 14:42.858
And you, you're more
of a woman

14:42.893 --> 14:45.444
than anyone else
in this room!

14:47.948 --> 14:49.315
Get him!

14:57.808 --> 15:01.710
Oh, honey, I'm so excited
to finally meet your girlfriend.

15:01.745 --> 15:02.978
Here she comes now.

15:03.013 --> 15:05.014
Yoo-hoo, baby!

15:05.048 --> 15:06.899
Oh, no!

15:13.057 --> 15:16.526
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return to Tom & Jerry:
The Final Episode.</i>

15:16.560 --> 15:17.794
So, that's it?
That's it.

15:17.828 --> 15:19.062
This is so much easier.

15:19.096 --> 15:21.164
I don't know why
I didn't do this years ago.

15:21.198 --> 15:23.266
What do you want me
to do with the body?

15:23.300 --> 15:25.235
(scoffs) I don't care.
Throw it in the garbage.

15:25.269 --> 15:27.036
Do you want any
of his oversized mallets?

15:27.071 --> 15:28.438
<i>I will take a mallet.</i>

15:28.472 --> 15:30.039
(phone rings)

15:30.074 --> 15:31.674
Ah, I gotta take this.

15:31.709 --> 15:32.742
Who's calling?

15:32.776 --> 15:34.010
My ex-girlfriend.

15:34.044 --> 15:35.845
She calls me drunk
every Valentine's Day.

15:35.880 --> 15:37.113
Hey, Samantha.

15:37.148 --> 15:40.783
Yeah, yeah, I'm sorry.
I still love Lois.

15:40.818 --> 15:43.153
Oh, come on. You would have
been a great mom.

15:43.187 --> 15:45.088
(whispering): She had cervical cancer
five years ago.

15:45.122 --> 15:47.557
She's basically a boob
on a leg at this point.

15:47.591 --> 15:48.825
Well, that's something.

15:48.859 --> 15:50.426
You're in a book club?

15:50.461 --> 15:52.362
Those are tough
to get into.

15:52.396 --> 15:54.314
What? Well,
I didn't even know

15:54.348 --> 15:56.649
the Fine Young Cannibals
were still together.

15:56.684 --> 15:57.951
Eight-city tour?

15:57.985 --> 15:59.986
Well, I don't know
if I can make eight,

16:00.020 --> 16:01.454
but I can certainly do six.

16:01.488 --> 16:02.455
<i>What about Lois?</i>

16:02.489 --> 16:03.940
She's totally out
of the picture.

16:03.974 --> 16:05.542
We've done everything
but sign the papers.

16:05.576 --> 16:08.044
Samantha, Samantha,
I will see you in Binghamton.

16:08.078 --> 16:10.496
And now I want you to go
and take a picture of yourself

16:10.530 --> 16:12.932
because it will be
your last day alone.

16:12.967 --> 16:14.834
Geez, what's not clear
about "Get lost"?

16:14.869 --> 16:17.403
By the way, my attendance
at home is gonna be spotty

16:17.438 --> 16:18.771
over the next few weeks.

16:21.525 --> 16:25.078
And, well, prize pumpkin
from the county fair,

16:25.112 --> 16:28.948
that's why I'm naming you
my Chief of Police.

16:28.983 --> 16:32.602
Mayor West, there's
something you need to see!

16:36.540 --> 16:40.510
My God! My wife is
seeing another mayor!

16:40.544 --> 16:41.978
I'm sorry, sir.

16:42.012 --> 16:45.498
Don't be. Because
I'm going to win her back.

16:45.532 --> 16:48.968
I trust you'll take care
of things here in my absence.

16:50.254 --> 16:51.654
Officer down!

16:54.508 --> 16:56.526
I hereby declare
this public park

16:56.560 --> 17:00.580
and future homosexual
meeting spot... open!

17:00.614 --> 17:02.899
Unhand that woman,
you bastard!

17:02.933 --> 17:04.567
(gasps) Adam!

17:04.602 --> 17:08.071
Well, well, well, if it isn't
Mayor "Guns For Toys" West.

17:08.105 --> 17:10.673
The chair recognizes
your face!

17:10.708 --> 17:12.725
<i>En garde!</i>

17:17.248 --> 17:18.348
Is the park open?

17:18.382 --> 17:19.699
Not yet!

17:23.921 --> 17:26.389
You call that kissing a baby?!

17:29.810 --> 17:31.561
That's how you kiss a baby.

17:35.783 --> 17:38.818
I hereby declare this
Stabby Eye Day!

17:38.852 --> 17:40.937
(screams)

17:40.988 --> 17:43.673
Oh, Adam, I'm so sorry!

17:43.707 --> 17:45.308
Carol, I love you

17:45.342 --> 17:46.876
and I can't live
without you.

17:46.910 --> 17:49.579
Please, never let this happen
again.

17:49.613 --> 17:50.813
I won't, Adam.

17:50.848 --> 17:54.384
You're the only mayor for me.

17:54.418 --> 17:57.553
Hey-ey, Carol.
I almost didn't recognize you

17:57.588 --> 18:00.456
without my special sauce
all over your face.

18:06.430 --> 18:09.065
Is somebody out there?

18:09.099 --> 18:10.633
Chris, it's me!

18:10.668 --> 18:12.268
Uncle Herbert's
grandniece, Sandy!

18:12.303 --> 18:14.604
Oh, hi, Sandy. What's up?

18:14.638 --> 18:16.272
(hushed):
What do I say?

18:16.307 --> 18:17.940
You say,
"Chris, I wanted

18:17.975 --> 18:20.276
to come see you
because, well..."

18:20.311 --> 18:24.113
Chris, I wanted to come
see you because, well...

18:24.148 --> 18:25.982
I'm kind of a
lonely old man.

18:26.016 --> 18:27.283
Really?

18:27.318 --> 18:30.353
Now, I know I'm not much
to look at,

18:30.387 --> 18:32.255
and ever since I got banned
from the arcade,

18:32.289 --> 18:33.523
I don't know what I'm doing.

18:33.557 --> 18:34.791
But if you're up for it,

18:34.825 --> 18:37.126
I'd like to spend some time
with you.

18:37.161 --> 18:38.745
Okay. Sure, Sandy!

18:38.779 --> 18:40.813
I'll come right down!

18:40.848 --> 18:41.864
Thanks, Uncle Herbert.

18:41.899 --> 18:44.100
I don't know how
I could ever repay you.

18:44.134 --> 18:46.636
Well, there
is one thing.

18:46.670 --> 18:48.588
(both laughing)

18:50.758 --> 18:53.426
Also, if I gave you
a sandwich,

18:53.460 --> 18:56.496
do you think you could
get Chris to fart on it?

18:59.683 --> 19:02.769
Well, guess
I better be going.

19:02.803 --> 19:04.670
I gotta get this heart
to Madonna.

19:04.705 --> 19:07.573
Oh, my God! Madonna needs
a heart transplant?

19:07.608 --> 19:09.542
No, she just doesn't want
other people

19:09.576 --> 19:11.144
to have them
for some reason.

19:11.178 --> 19:13.646
But before I go... Here.

19:13.680 --> 19:16.049
For me?

19:16.083 --> 19:17.533
My kidney!

19:17.568 --> 19:18.935
I wanted you to have it.

19:18.969 --> 19:22.055
Oh, Toby, I love it!
Thank you.

19:22.089 --> 19:24.957
This has been the best
Valentine's Day ever.

19:32.983 --> 19:34.417
Oh, Peter, it was fun

19:34.451 --> 19:36.185
spending the day
in bed with you.

19:36.220 --> 19:37.787
It sure was, Lois.

19:37.821 --> 19:40.022
Happy Valentine's Day.

19:43.410 --> 19:45.678
Hey, Lois,
remember our wedding?

19:45.712 --> 19:47.580
Yeah, I sure do.

19:47.614 --> 19:49.115
Remember the dance?

19:49.149 --> 19:50.683
Of course I do, Peter.

19:50.717 --> 19:52.118
Who was that
half-Persian chick

19:52.152 --> 19:53.586
who was dancing
with your cousin?

19:53.620 --> 19:55.221
I think her name
was Flora.

19:55.255 --> 19:56.322
Yeah... yeah.

19:56.356 --> 19:58.241
Okay, all right,
I'm ready! I'm ready!

19:58.275 --> 20:00.042
What?
Shut up for ten minutes

20:00.077 --> 20:02.378
and pretend we're in the back
behind the speakers.

20:02.413 --> 20:04.046
(moaning)

20:04.081 --> 20:07.049
This wedding sucks, huh?

20:07.084 --> 20:08.634
♪

20:12.423 --> 20:18.394
♪ L is for the way
you look at me ♪

20:18.429 --> 20:24.434
♪ O is for the only one I see

20:24.468 --> 20:31.056
♪ V is very, very
extraordinary ♪

20:31.074 --> 20:37.480
♪ E is even more than anyone
that you adore can ♪

20:37.514 --> 20:43.135
♪ Love is all
that I can give to you ♪

20:43.542 --> 20:49.080
♪ Love is more than just
a game for two ♪

20:49.517 --> 20:53.034
♪ Two in love can make it

20:53.134 --> 20:55.602
♪ Take my heart
and please don't break it... ♪

20:59.382 --> 21:01.849
(screaming)

21:01.850 --> 22:02.850
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru